# A machine never starts again a journal whose booking it released once,
# also when the coordinator books it there again. The machine reported the
# stop, so the "left pool" excuse holds for it, but the registry books it:
# the journal runs a member short while the cell believes it serves.
# The fixed-seed hunt caught it on some heads only (#845 (fix-main)) until
# the regrown-journal scenario (#1003 (uncounted skips from fix-main)): a
# tail step shrinks a journal to one acceptor and grows it back, so a
# released machine is booked again. With the mutant, 20 of 600 hunt seeds
# went red ("leads: a created journal the cell can hold takes a write after
# chaos" and "controls: every control journal runs on its booked machines
# after chaos"), and the widened journal never started again on a released
# member on the 30 seeds that shrank one.
excuse: node: left pool
expect: caught
file: crates/lib/paros-roles/src/node/control.rs
--- find
        for journal in booked {
--- replace
        for journal in booked {
            if self.journals.released(journal) {
                continue;
            }
--- end
